P(f"Moran's I of the landslide label was {lab[0.25]:.2f} at 0–0.5 km, {lab[2.5]:.2f} at 2–3 km, {lab[6.25]:.2f} at 5–7.5 km and {lab[8.75]:.2f} at 7.5–10 km, and it was indistinguishable from zero beyond 10 km (Figure 3). Smooth fields such as rainfall and sand content stayed autocorrelated to about 10 km, whereas TWI and distance to road decorrelated within 2–3 km.")
