H2('4.5. Statistical Comparison of Models')
DT = T['D']
def drow(a, b):
    d = DT[(DT.A == a) & (DT.B == b)]
    return d
pairs = [('XGBoost', 'RF'), ('XGBoost', 'GBM'), ('XGBoost', 'SVM'), ('RF', 'GBM'), ('RF', 'SVM'), ('GBM', 'SVM'), ('Ensemble-equal', 'RF'), ('Ensemble-equal', 'XGBoost'), ('Ensemble-equal', 'GBM'), ('Ensemble-equal', 'SVM'), ('Ensemble-equal', 'Best single (inner-CV)'), ('Ensemble-stacked', 'Ensemble-equal')]
rows = []
for a, b in pairs:
    d = drow(a, b)
    r0 = d[d.rep == 0].iloc[0]
    rows.append([f"{mlabel.get(a,a)} − {mlabel.get(b,b)}", f"{r0['diff']:+.4f} [{r0.diff_lo:+.4f}, {r0.diff_hi:+.4f}]", f"{r0.p_holm:.3f}" if r0.p_holm >= 0.001 else '<0.001',
                 f"{(d.p_holm < 0.05).sum()} of {len(d)}"])
TAB('**Table 7.** Model T: pairwise DeLong tests on pooled out-of-fold predictions. The AUC difference and its 95% confidence interval and the Holm-adjusted p value are shown for the first repeat; the last column counts the repeats in which the adjusted p value was below 0.05.',
    ['Comparison', 'ΔAUC [95% CI], repeat 1', 'Holm-adjusted p, repeat 1', 'Significant repeats'], rows,
    'Holm correction was applied over the thirteen comparisons made in each repeat (the AUC-weighted versus equal-weight comparison, which differed by <0.0001, is listed in Supplementary Table S4).')
sig_pairs = [(a, b) for a, b in pairs[:6] if (drow(a, b).p_holm < 0.05).sum() >= 2]
P(f"Differences in AUC among the four single models were small, at most {max(abs(drow(a,b)['diff']).max() for a,b in pairs[:6]):.3f} (Table 7). " +
  (f"Only {', '.join(f'{mlabel.get(a,a)} versus {mlabel.get(b,b)}' for a,b in sig_pairs)} remained significant after Holm correction in at least two of three repeats; " if sig_pairs else "No pairwise difference among the single models remained significant after Holm correction in two or more of the three repeats; ") +
  f"differences changed sign between repeats, that is, with the way regions were allocated to folds. The equal-weight ensemble, by contrast, exceeded each single model in every repeat, by {DT[(DT.A=='Ensemble-equal')&DT.B.isin(['RF','XGBoost','GBM','SVM'])]['diff'].min():.3f}–{DT[(DT.A=='Ensemble-equal')&DT.B.isin(['RF','XGBoost','GBM','SVM'])]['diff'].max():.3f} AUC; the gain was significant after Holm correction against {', '.join(f'{k} ({v} of 3 repeats)' for k,v in esig.items())}, and beat the inner-CV \"best single\" strategy significantly in {(drow('Ensemble-equal','Best single (inner-CV)').p_holm < 0.05).sum()} of 3. Neither stacking nor AUC weighting improved significantly on equal weights in any repeat. The ranking reported in the original submission (XGBoost significantly best) does not hold under spatial validation.")

H2('4.6. What Agreement and Dispersion Say about Error')
